---An export policy rule describing various export options.
---@class gcp.netapp_v1.SimpleExportPolicyRule
---@field squashMode? gcp.netapp_v1.SimpleExportPolicyRuleSquashModeEnum|string Optional. Defines how user identity squashing is applied for this export rule. This field is the preferred way to configure squashing behavior and takes precedence over `has_root_access` if both are provided.
---@field kerberos5iReadOnly? boolean If enabled (true) the rule defines a read only access for clients matching the 'allowedClients' specification. It enables nfs clients to mount using 'integrity' kerberos security mode.
---@field kerberos5pReadOnly? boolean If enabled (true) the rule defines a read only access for clients matching the 'allowedClients' specification. It enables nfs clients to mount using 'privacy' kerberos security mode.
---@field nfsv4? boolean NFS V4 protocol.
---@field kerberos5pReadWrite? boolean If enabled (true) the rule defines read and write access for clients matching the 'allowedClients' specification. It enables nfs clients to mount using 'privacy' kerberos security mode. The 'kerberos5pReadOnly' value be ignored if this is enabled.
---@field allowedClients? string Comma separated list of allowed clients IP addresses
---@field anonUid? string Optional. An integer representing the anonymous user ID. Range is 0 to `4294967295`. Required when `squash_mode` is `ROOT_SQUASH` or `ALL_SQUASH`.
